POPULATION
Population growth
On Census Day, 21 November 2021, the usual resident population in Malta stood at 519,562, more than doubling over a century.  
Since the last Census, the population grew by more than 100,000 from 417,432 residents in 2011 – this is equal to a 24.5 per 
cent increase over just 10 years. This is the largest intercensal growth ever recorded to date, resulting from a steady growth of 
approximately 10,000 residents per year over the last 10 years.  Prior to the 2021 Census, the largest ever recorded average 
intercensal growth was between 1931 and 1948, where it stood at 3,786 persons per year.
